[Music]  on this Mother's Day weekend we have a  very special Saturday session last month  Carnegie Hall released the album hopes  and dreams the lullaby project 12  lullabies performed by some of the  biggest names in music including Fiona  Apple rosanne Cash and Rhiannon Giddens  but the songs were co-written by  amateurs expectant mothers with no  songwriting experience you'll hear two  of those amazing lullabies performed  here in studio 57 shortly  the first here's Michelle Miller in the  time spent waiting for a sonogram  appointment we expected parents did  something that blew their minds writing  their unborn baby a lullaby so far so  good we was like thinking like we can't  really write a song you know like the  experience is given to parents once a  week here at the Jacobi Medical Center  in the Bronx he'll listen to it as a  baby and he'll always remember that it's  both of us like what we feel and how we  thought about him before he was born  yeah you know like that's always gonna  be like a family thing their teachers  Carnegie Hall musicians Marika Hughes  and Deirdre Rodman struck begin the  process asking parents to compose a  letter to their child which is used for  the lyrics then they practice practice  practice in a matter of a few hours  they produce melodies for three moms in  a dad personalizing each to the parents  pitch passion do you speak any other  languages Arabic Arabic even the  language of their choice I have a secret  history as a composer of lullabies the  lullaby project is the baby of Carnegie  Hall's Thomas cabinets when I was a  young musician in New York and I had no  money I had a friend whose wife was  expecting they were going to have a  child and I decided since I didn't have  anything else to give them that I would  write a lullaby for the baby  I loved writing the lullaby I loved  being able to give it to them as a gift  [Music]  cabinets thought composing a lullaby  would be good for first-time parents  especially those insecure over being too  young or having to go it alone what can  you say to people in the greater  understanding of what this does and what  this means it's in the songs you can  hear it in the music that they create so  to me that's where the evidence is in  the last six and a half years his  project has produced more than 800  lullabies songwriting he says is a gift  of healing and connection it's expanded  to shelters and correctional facilities  [Music]  this year those songs turned into a  professionally produced album featuring  some of the biggest voices in music  Patti LuPone Dianne Reeves Catherine  zeta-jones how did you get folks to sign  on board well we were very lucky Joyce  DiDonato who is a big metropolitan opera  star heard about our work and came and  sang with us on a concert and she  invited a record producer he said I bet  I can persuade my friends and their  friends to come in and sing these  lullabies because they're amazing  they're beautiful and people should hear  them at first I thought what am I gonna  do one of the songs is peace it brings  me joy written at Jacobi Medical Center  five years ago by tamela's Fernandez for  her son Lavie I was just excited to have  a song that I could show him from when I  was carrying him and she's proud that  her words may one day helped to spark a  movement what would it mean if having a  lullaby was just part of the the birth  process we're hopeful that the partners  who come together with us will honestly  they'll help us create a kind of lullaby  movement because that would be amazing  [Music]

